<title>MEXICO: Mexico's ports all reopened as winds reside - gov't.</title>
<headline>Mexico's ports all reopened as winds reside - gov't.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>All of Mexico's ports were open Thursday as of 10 local/1600 GMT as the strong winds that had closed ports all week eased up, the Communications and Transport ministry said in its meteorological report.</p>
<p>Smaller ships are still restricted from sailing from Progreso and Frontera ports along the Carribean Sea and Salina Cruz in the Pacific because of moderate winds.</p>
<p>Crude oil ports opened Wednesday after being shut for three days.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903</p>
</text>
